@startuml Receiver Registration

title Receiver registration gates destinations, departure and declarations
caption Target design. Decisions D22, D30, D35, D33, P11. ADR 0012.

autonumber

actor Administrator as admin
actor "Ground Officer" as go
actor Dispatcher as disp
participant "Freedom API" as api
database "dbo.Receiver" as rcv
database "sensitive.ReceiverDetail" as sens

go -> api : create Receiver (organisation, region)
api -> rcv : Receiver, status **Pending**
go -> api : record delivery address and contact
api -> sens : ReceiverDetail (Ground Officer only)

disp -> api : make Receiver a box destination
api -> rcv : status?
api --> disp : 409, not registered

admin -> api : PUT /receivers/{ref}/status Registered
note right of admin
  Only the Administrator changes status.
  Nothing records **what kind of body** a Receiver is (D33).
end note
api -> rcv : status Registered

disp -> api : make Receiver a box destination
api --> disp : ok
disp -> api : set Receiver as a vehicle's handover Receiver
api --> disp : ok

== Suspension ==
admin -> api : GET /receivers/{ref}/usage
api --> admin : convoys and boxes allocated (counts and ids, no address)
admin -> api : PUT /receivers/{ref}/status Suspended
api -> rcv : status Suspended
note over api
  Boxes and vehicles allocated to it now fail a blocking requirement,
  and declarations naming it become stale: the convoy cannot depart
  until they are reallocated or the Receiver is registered again.
end note

@enduml
